e of Oceania, the narrative unfolds in a post-World War II world, reflecting the anxieties of the Cold War era. Orwell, whose real name was Eric Arthur Blair, wrote this work in 1948, and it has since become a seminal text in political literature, influencing discussions about freedom, privacy, and authority across the globe.

